// Auto-generated from the clinic's DSM-5-TR classification appendix, translated
// to Spanish (standard clinical terminology) since that's the working language
// at the clinic. Code + name lookup only (not diagnostic criteria) — used to show
// the ICD-10-CM code next to a diagnosis for cleaner record-keeping.
// Regenerate via the extraction/translation script in the project notes if
// corrections are needed — most entries are literal, but the substance-induced
// disorder tail (alcohol/cannabis/opioid/etc.) was generated by template and may
// read a little mechanically; flag anything wrong and it's a one-line fix.
//
// Cross-checked against Diego's physical copy of the official APA Spanish
// translation ("Guía de consulta de los criterios diagnósticos del DSM-5",
// 2013) — 43 entries corrected to match its wording (mostly word-order
// conventions Spanish clinical usage actually follows, e.g. "Trastorno de la
// Personalidad Paranoide" not "Trastorno Paranoide de la Personalidad").
// Deliberately NOT changed: entries where DSM-5-TR (2022, this file's
// original English source) updated the diagnosis/terminology/code after the
// 2013 book was published — e.g. Prolonged Grief Disorder (F43.8) didn't
// exist in 2013; "Provisional Tic Disorder" (F95.0) was "Transient" in 2013;
// some substance-use ICD-10-CM codes were revised between editions. Using
// the older book's text there would be a regression, not a correction.
export interface Dsm5Entry {
  code: string;
  name: string;
}

